{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The whole fee rests on the driver's arrival, and that arrival rests on one carrier only. The trip record's own marker reads 'Driver GPS within 10m of pickup point. Speed 0 km/h. Auto-arrival confirmed.' — it was generated from the driver's own GPS fix — so under POL-GEN-02 the marker and the GPS trace are one carrier rather than two independent ones, and POL-NS-21's requirement that the arrival be corroborated by the trace is satisfied by nothing outside itself. Taking the nearest fix at its reported position, as the policy directs for a fix that reports no accuracy, the 0.0 m distance is measured inside that same carrier. The carrier is IMPAIRED: EV-GPS-00903 carries weight_multiplier 0.6 with issue codes LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD, on 8 fixes with 5 gaps longer than 120 s, so it cannot reliably establish the arrival the fee depends on.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00903", "EV-GPS-00903"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.derived.arrival_check",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "The 5-minute free wait runs, under POL-NS-21, from 'the driver's arrival at the pickup', and POL-NS-22 makes the fee chargeable only '[w]hen the driver cancels after the free wait'. The start of that clock is carried only by EV-GPS-00903, which is IMPAIRED at weight_multiplier 0.6 with issue codes LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD; the platform's arithmetic (arrival 08:43, wait ends 08:48, cancellation 08:51) is therefore built on a premise this record does not reliably establish, and the rider should not be made to carry a fee whose trigger is unproven.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00903", "EV-GPS-00903", "EV-FARE-00903"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21", "POL-NS-22"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.free_wait",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "This is the open question POL-GEN-26 is written for. Whether, and when, the driver was at the pickup cannot be settled, because the evidence that would carry it — EV-GPS-00903, IMPAIRED, weight_multiplier 0.6, issue codes LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD — is in any event the same carrier as the marker it is offered to corroborate. POL-GEN-26 directs that where such a fact cannot be established the case is escalated and the open question stated, with no outcome inferred from the absence; the 5.00 is then held rather than collected from the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00903", "EV-TRIP-00903"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-26", "POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.derived.arrival_check",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's profile carries fraud_flags of 1, so POL-GEN-22 fixes the confidence an AI ruling needs at 0.95. POL-GEN-02(2) forbids the judge's confidence from exceeding the lowest weight_multiplier among the artifacts carrying the deciding fact, and the deciding fact — the driver's arrival — is carried only by EV-GPS-00903 at weight_multiplier 0.6 (IMPAIRED, issue codes LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD), the marker not being independent of it. The ceiling on any AI ruling here is therefore 0.6, far below 0.95, and that gap cannot be closed by argument; POL-GEN-22 requires the case to go to a human reviewer rather than be decided below its threshold.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00903", "EV-GPS-00903"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-22", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.fraud_flags",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's account — at the pickup point at Tiong Bahru Plaza on time, unable to find the car — is not contradicted anywhere on this record. No counterparty statement is on file, EV-GPS-00903 carries no rider track at all, and no artifact records the rider's absence from the pickup, so the 'rider_no_show' designation rests on the driver-side trace alone (EV-GPS-00903, IMPAIRED, weight_multiplier 0.6, issue codes LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD). A no-show that is not made out on evidence is not a basis for charging the rider under POL-NS-22, and the unresolved question is one POL-GEN-26 sends to a human reviewer.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00903", "EV-TRIP-00903", "EV-CHAT-00903"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-22", "POL-GEN-26"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing in the rider's history can supply what the evidence lacks. Under POL-GEN-01 the rider's rating (3.9), prior_disputes_filed (4), prior_disputes_upheld (1) and prior_no_show_flags (1) are CONTEXT ONLY and may never establish a fact about this trip or decide its outcome, and the one rider counter POL-NS-25 names, no_show_cancellations_30d, is null on this record, so its referral cannot be made either.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00903"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-01", "POL-NS-25"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 5.00,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 5.00,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Rider R-7823, your $5.00 no-show fee stands; Driver D-2398, that $5.00 is confirmed to you as compensation.\n\nThe record shows the driver reached Tiong Bahru Plaza at 08:43:00 — before the 08:50:00 deadline (scheduled 08:45:00 plus 5 minutes), so POL-NS-24's free-cancellation right does not arise and no FULL_REFUND or goodwill credit follows from it. The POL-NS-21 free wait ran 300 s from that arrival, to 08:48:00, and the driver cancelled at 08:51:00, after both the free wait and the 8-minute no-show threshold. Before cancelling, the driver sent in-app messages at 08:43:00, 08:45:20, 08:49:30 and 08:50:45 and placed an in-app call at 08:47:05 (rang 22 s, unanswered) — every one before the 08:51:00 cancellation — so POL-NS-23's contact obligation is met and no refund follows from it either. The fee of 5.00 SGD equals the fee fixed for this trip (POL-NS-22), so the amount-charged referral is not triggered.\n\nOn your account that the driver never appeared: the arrival is established. The trip record's arrival event is corroborated by the GPS trace, and the same fact is carried independently by the driver's own contemporaneous in-app messages of 08:43:00 and 08:45:20. I note that EV-GPS-00903 is impaired — weight 0.6, issue codes LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD — and that the trip record's arrival marker is auto-generated from that same trace, so marker and trace are one carrier and do not corroborate each other; but EV-CHAT-00903 is a complete artifact (weight 1.0) whose messages carry the arrival independently, so under POL-GEN-02(2) the fact is not confined to the impaired trace and the confidence ceiling is 1.0, not 0.6.\n\nYour profile carries fraud_flags of 1, so POL-GEN-22 requires confidence of 0.95 for this ruling; that bar is reachable only because of the independent carrier above, and is met. Under POL-GEN-01 the rest of your profile history (rating, prior_disputes_filed, prior_disputes_upheld, prior_no_show_flags) is context only and decides nothing. POL-GEN-26 is not engaged: the facts the no-show rules need — the arrival, the free-wait expiry, the message and the call before cancellation, and the amount charged — are all established on complete artifacts; the missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00903-01, weight 0.0) carries no fact and nothing needed rests on it. The rider's no_show_cancellations_30d counter is absent from the profile, so POL-NS-25 raises no repeat-no-show referral. POL-NS-26 makes the AI ruling final on this no-show, and the value (5.00 SGD) is below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD human-review threshold.\n\nOutcome: your claim is not supported and the present charge stands. Under POL-NS-22 and POL-GEN-03 the ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, moving 5.00 SGD to the driver, with amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both 5.00 SGD."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.6,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute is about the 5.00 SGD no-show fee charged on trip TRIP-2026-09945. The rider filed it and asked for the 5.00 SGD to be reversed. That request cannot be granted, and the fee cannot be confirmed either, so the case goes to a human reviewer with the 5.00 SGD held rather than collected or refunded.\n\nWhat the record does establish. The driver's contact obligation under POL-NS-23 is met: the chat log (EV-CHAT-00903) carries the driver's in-app messages at 08:43:00, 08:45:20, 08:49:30 and 08:50:45, and the trip record (EV-TRIP-00903) carries an in-app call placed by the driver at 08:47:05 — both limbs, both before the 08:51:00 cancellation. POL-NS-24 is not engaged: the scheduled pickup was 08:45:00, the deadline was 08:50:00, and the arrival is recorded at 08:43:00, so the rider's free-cancellation right and the 5.00 SGD goodwill credit do not arise. The ledger (EV-FARE-00903) charges exactly 5.00 SGD, the fee the policy fixes, so POL-NS-22's amount-check referral does not fire, and POL-NS-25's repeat no-show referral cannot be made because rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d is null (POL-GEN-01).\n\nWhat cannot be established to the required confidence. The fee stands or falls on the driver's arrival at the pickup — the fact POL-NS-21 and POL-NS-22 read (the free wait runs from the arrival; the fee is chargeable when the driver cancels after it). On this record that fact is carried by the driver's own GPS measurement: the trip record's driver_arrived marker at 08:43:00 was auto-confirmed from that measurement, so under POL-GEN-02 the marker and the GPS trace EV-GPS-00903 are one carrier, not two, and the arrival test's corroboration comes from nothing outside the marker itself. That carrier is impaired: EV-GPS-00903 carries weight_multiplier 0.6 with issue codes LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD (five of seven gaps exceed 120 s, and the waiting window holds fewer than the six fixes POL-NS-08(b) requires). The rider's point that the arrival rests on this carrier is well taken; the driver's contrary point, that the needed facts sit on COMPLETE 1.0 artifacts, does not hold for the arrival, because the trip-record marker is the same carrier as the trace. The driver's chat is genuine contemporaneous evidence, but it is the driver's own account of the very fact in dispute and repeats what the marker already records, so it does not independently carry the arrival so as to lift the cap. The rider's own account is likewise not an independent carrier.\n\nConsequence. rider_profile.fraud_flags is 1, so POL-GEN-22, and POL-NS-26 on top of it, fix the confidence an AI ruling needs at 0.95. POL-GEN-02(2) caps confidence at the weight of the artifact carrying the deciding fact — 0.6 here — and POL-GEN-26 directs that a fact a rule needs, which impaired evidence cannot establish, goes to a human reviewer with the open question stated. Ruling: ESCALATE; the 5.00 SGD is held.\n\nOpen question for the reviewer: whether the driver was at the pickup at 08:43:00 on 2026-09-13, given that the auto-arrival marker and the impaired GPS trace are one and the same carrier."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
